
1. Create lab folder and files

PS> cd C:\bda-labs
PS> mkdir lab2-hdfs
PS> cd lab2-hdfs
PS> notepad docker-compose.yml

docker-compose.yml:

services:
  namenode:
    image: apache/hadoop:3.3.6
    hostname: namenode
    command: ["hdfs", "namenode"]
    ports:
      - "9870:9870"
    env_file: ./config
    environment:
      ENSURE_NAMENODE_DIR: "/tmp/hadoop-root/dfs/name"
  datanode:
    image: apache/hadoop:3.3.6
    command: ["hdfs", "datanode"]
    env_file: ./config

Create the config:

PS> notepad config

config:

CORE-SITE.XML_fs.default.name=hdfs://namenode
CORE-SITE.XML_fs.defaultFS=hdfs://namenode
HDFS-SITE.XML_dfs.namenode.rpc-address=namenode:8020
HDFS-SITE.XML_dfs.replication=1

2. Launch and format

PS> docker compose up -d

Wait ~15 seconds:

PS> docker compose exec namenode bash

Inside the container:

hadoop@namenode:~$ hdfs dfs -mkdir -p /user/student
hadoop@namenode:~$ hdfs dfs -ls /user

3. Create the Java program

hadoop@namenode:~$ nano HdfsDemo.java

Paste the Java code from your lab manual here.

4. Compile and package

hadoop@namenode:~$ export HADOOP_CLASSPATH=$(hadoop classpath)
hadoop@namenode:~$ mkdir classes
hadoop@namenode:~$ javac -classpath $HADOOP_CLASSPATH -d classes HdfsDemo.java
hadoop@namenode:~$ jar -cvf hdfsdemo.jar -C classes .

5. Run it

hadoop@namenode:~$ hadoop jar hdfsdemo.jar HdfsDemo

Expected output:

Wrote file: /user/student/quangle.txt
From start : On the top of the Crumpetty Tree
After seek : The Quangle Wangle sat
Length : 56 bytes
Replication: 1
--- listStatus /user/student ---
quangle.txt
--- globStatus *.txt ---
quangle.txt

6. Confirm the file is on HDFS

hadoop@namenode:~$ hdfs dfs -cat /user/student/quangle.txt

7. Add second file and re-run

hadoop@namenode:~$ echo "hello hdfs" | hdfs dfs -put - /user/student/notes.txt
hadoop@namenode:~$ hadoop jar hdfsdemo.jar HdfsDemo

8. Clean up

hadoop@namenode:~$ exit

Back in PowerShell:

PS> docker compose down